      {
        "title":"",
        "phase": '<p class="dmn"><b>Domain 10: Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplant, Principles and Products, Stem Cell Source and Dose</b></p><p class="ans-txt"><b>Peripheral blood stem cells (PBSCs).</b> The following table compares the characteristics of PBSC and umbilical cord blood (UCB):</p><table class="table"><tr><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>Characteristic</b></p></td><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>PBSC</b></p></td><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>UCB</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Fastest engraftment</p></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td><td><p class="P_T" /></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Slowest engraftment</p></td><td><p class="P_T" /></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Slowest immune reconstitution</p></td><td><p class="P_T" /></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Highest incidence of graft-vs-host disease (GvHD)</p></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td><td><p class="P_T" /></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Readily/rapidly available</p></td><td><p class="P_T" /></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Can be collected and cryopreserved in advance</p></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td><td><p class="td_p">&#x2713;</p></td></tr></table><p class="ans-txt">PBSCs are the fastest engrafting stem cell source</p><div class="key"><p><b>Key Point:</b> PBSCs engraft the fastest; however, all stem cell sources have risks and benefits.</p></div><div class="suggested_readings"><p><u>Suggested Readings</u></p><p>Jacobson CA, Turki AT, McDonough SM, et al. Immune reconstitution after double umbilical cord blood stem cell transplantation: comparison with unrelated peripheral blood stem cell transplantation. <i>Biol Blood Marrow Transplant</i>. 2012;18(4):565-574. doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbmt.2011.08.018">10.1016/j.bbmt.2011.08.018</a></p><p>Lacan C, Lambert J, Forcade E, et al. Bone marrow graft versus peripheral blood graft in haploidentical hematopoietic stem cells transplantation: a retrospective analysis in 1344 patients of SFGM-TC registry. <i>J Hematol Oncol</i>. 2024;17(1):2. doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s13045-023-01515-4">10.1186/s13045-023-01515-4</a></p></div>'
      }
