        "title":"",
        "phase": '<p class="dmn"><b>Domain 10: Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplant, Principles and Products, Stem Cell Source and Dose</b></p><table class="table"><tr><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>Cell Product</b></p></td><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>Cell Dose</b></p></td><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>Characteristics</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">PBSCs</p></td><td><p class="td_p">2-4&#x00A0;&#x00D7;&#x00A0;10<sup>6</sup> CD34+ cells/kg</p></td><td><p class="td_p">Fast engraftment</p><p class="td_p">Lower primary graft failure</p><p class="td_p">Increased GvHD in allogeneic transplantation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">Bone marrow</p></td><td><p class="td_p">2-4&#x00A0;&#x00D7;&#x00A0;10<sup>8</sup> total nucleated cells (TNC)/kg</p></td><td><p class="td_p">Slower engraftment compared to PBSC</p><p class="td_p">Lower GvHD risk compared to PBSC</p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">UCB</p></td><td><p class="td_p">2-4&#x00A0;&#x00D7;&#x00A0;10<sup>7</sup> TNC/kg</p><p class="td_p">and</p><p class="td_p">&#x003E;1.5&#x00A0;&#x00D7;&#x00A0;10<sup>6</sup> CD34/kg</p></td><td><p class="td_p">Cell dose is fixed and limited. Donor is not available/accessible for future stem cell donations.</p><p class="td_p">Can use 2 cord blood units (double cord transplant) to target cumulative cell dose</p></td></tr></table><div class="key"><p><b>Key Point:</b> There are different stem cell sources available for transplantation, each has unique characteristics.</p></div><div class="suggested_readings"><p><u>Suggested Readings</u></p><p>Barker JN, Weisdorf DJ, DeFor TE, et al. Transplantation of 2 partially HLA-matched umbilical cord blood units to enhance engraftment in adults with hematologic malignancy. <i>Blood</i>. 2005 Feb 1;105(3):1343-7. doi: 10.1182/blood-2004-07-2717. Epub 2004 Oct 5. PMID: 15466923.</p><p>Dehn J, Spellman S, Hurley CK, et al. Selection of unrelated donors and cord blood units for hematopoietic cell transplantation: guidelines from the NMDP/CIBMTR. <i>Blood</i>. 2019;134(12):924-934. doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.1182/blood.2019001212">10.1182/blood.2019001212</a></p></div>'
